            "heading": "\"Diploma\" Still Sounds Like a Backup Plan",
            "kind": "items",
            "items": [
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "\"Just do a degree, a diploma looks weak on a resume.\""
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "\"Any diploma is basically the same, just pick the cheapest one nearby.\""
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "\"Diplomas are only for students who could not get into a good degree college.\""
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "\"Private diploma colleges with '100% placement' banners are automatically a safe bet.\""
              }
            ],
            "sourceSectionId": "why",
            "sourceNeedIndex": 1
          },
          {
            "needId": "checklist:2",
            "type": "checklist",
            "heading": "Counts As a Diploma After 12th",
            "kind": "items",
            "items": [
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "Examples: Polytechnic engineering diplomas, D.Pharm, most paramedical diplomas."
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "Regulator: AICTE, state technical education boards, or the relevant health/pharmacy council."
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "Why it matters: These carry formal recognition for government jobs, licensing, and lateral entry into degrees."
              }
            ],
            "sourceSectionId": "what-counts",
            "sourceNeedIndex": 2
          },
          {
            "needId": "checklist:6",
            "type": "checklist",
            "heading": "Diploma After 12th Science",
            "kind": "items",
            "items": [
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "PCM: engineering diplomas (mechanical, civil, electrical, CS/IT) are the direct-fit route."
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "PCB: DMLT, GNM nursing, D.Pharm, physiotherapy, and optometry diplomas use your biology base directly."
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "Both PCM and PCB students can also enter digital, business, or design diplomas without restriction."
              }
            ],
            "sourceSectionId": "stream",
            "sourceNeedIndex": 6
          },
          {
            "needId": "checklist:12",
            "type": "checklist",
            "heading": "Bridge Back to a Full Degree",
            "kind": "items",
            "items": [
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "Minimum marks: At least 45% aggregate across all years of the diploma (40% for SC/ST candidates) under current AICTE norms."
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "Branch match required: Many colleges prefer a related branch for lateral entry, but rules differ by state and college."
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "Dedicated seats: Most states reserve roughly 10-15% of each B.Tech branch's approved intake specifically for lateral-entry diploma and BSc holders."
              }
            ],
            "sourceSectionId": "lateral-entry",
            "sourceNeedIndex": 12
          },
